<!--
    Generated from the VID/PID tables in core/backends/android/backend.cpp.
    Keep the two in sync: this file decides which devices Android offers to open
    SDR++ for (and auto-grants permission to), backend.cpp decides which module
    is allowed to claim the resulting file descriptor.

    Values MUST be decimal. android.hardware.usb.DeviceFilter.read() parses these
    with radix 10 unless the value carries an explicit 0x prefix, and it swallows
    the NumberFormatException, leaving the field at -1, which matches() treats as
    a wildcard. Bare hex like vendor-id="1d50" therefore silently becomes "any",
    which is how this file used to claim every USB device attached to the phone.

    No padding inside the quotes either: Integer.parseInt does not trim, so a
    trailing space throws and produces the same silent wildcard.
-->
